---
description: codesight-hooks active — native Grep/Glob/exploration-Bash are hard-blocked
alwaysApply: true
---

codesight-hooks are active in this workspace. Native `Grep`, `Glob`, and
code-exploration `Bash` calls (grep/rg/find/cat/head/tail/less/more/wc/awk/sed)
are intercepted and **blocked** — the hook returns `permissionDecision: deny`
with a pointer to the right codesight-mcp tool. Safe Bash (git/cargo/npm/docker/
pytest/build tools) passes through unchanged.

`Read` is **not** intercepted. Claude's Edit/Write tools require a prior Read
in session state, so blocking Read breaks the edit flow. Prefer codesight-mcp's
structured retrieval (`inspect_structure view=file_outline`, `read_content` with
explicit ranges, `get_symbol_source`) when you don't need the full file.

When a hook blocks a call, follow the `additionalContext` the block carries —
it names the specific codesight-mcp tool that covers the same intent.
